<urn:atm:triage:finding/AW3-CI-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AW3-CI-002" ;
  triage:title "arch-gates al8 and av3 boundary tests fail on AW.3: replacement runtime maintenance registration no longer detected, and doctor read-handler allowlist rejects DiagnosticCounters/DiagnosticCountersSource" ;
  triage:description "PR #1182 CI arch-gates (crates/atm-architecture/tests/boundary_enforcement.rs) fails two tests that PASS on integrate/phase-aw ffd78e16f: (1) boundary_enforcement.rs:3087 al8_replacement_runtime_registers_maintenance_for_every_composed_runtime_maintenance_implementer: start_replacement_runtime builds HttpRuntimeBuilder but never registers the router as the HttpRuntime maintenance object, so any RuntimeMaintenance implementer composed into StorageAndNudgeRouter (e.g. HerdrQueueWakePump) would silently never run; the AW.3 edit to crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/lib.rs (91 lines changed) broke this composition or the pattern the gate matches. Verify the maintenance registration is really wired, not just re-matched. (2) boundary_enforcement.rs:4040 av3_post_cutover_read_handlers_reject_legacy_blocking_dependencies: read-handler doctor allowlist rejects unlisted types DiagnosticCounters, DiagnosticCountersSource. Either add the two types to the doctor read-handler allowlist in the gate (they are non-blocking counters) or route them so the doctor handler does not take them directly. Reproduce: cargo test -p atm-architecture --test boundary_enforcement -- al8_replacement av3_post_cutover." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-aw" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "arch-gate" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-05T04:15:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AW3 ;
